From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rust_builder/linux: build the Rust library with plain cargo, not cargokit

Class:   LOCAL WORKAROUND (distro packaging; modelled on nixpkgs'
         pkgs/by-name/lo/localsend/no-cargokit.patch). Not for upstream:
         LocalSend upstream wants cargokit for its own CI and for users with
         rustup.
Applies: localsend v1.18.2 (patch -p1 from the repository root).
Fixes:   On a distro toolchain (Arch's `rust`, no rustup), `flutter build linux`
         fails inside cargokit, which
           - runs `rustup toolchain list` / `rustup run 1.97.1 cargo ...` and
             would `rustup toolchain install` the rust-toolchain.toml pin
             (1.97.1; the system has 1.99.1),
           - runs `dart pub get` for its own build_tool (network at build time),
           - maps FLUTTER_TARGET_PLATFORM to a triple through a table with no
             ppc64le entry ("Unknown target platform: linux-ppc64").
         The AUR recipe works around the first point with a fake `rustup`
         script on PATH; this replaces cargokit outright.

After this patch rust_builder/linux/CMakeLists.txt does one of two things:
  1. LOCALSEND_RUST_LIB set (environment or -D): bundle that prebuilt
     librust_lib_localsend_app.so as is. This is what the PKGBUILD uses: it
     runs `cargo build --frozen --release -p rust_lib_localsend_app --target
     powerpc64le-unknown-linux-gnu` itself, so makepkg's RUSTFLAGS/CFLAGS
     (and the baseline pool's -C target-cpu=pwr8) apply, and it can ISA-scan
     the library before Flutter ever sees it.
  2. Otherwise run `cargo build --locked --offline [--release] -p
     rust_lib_localsend_app --target <triple>` here, with cargo from PATH,
     triple from FLUTTER_TARGET_PLATFORM (linux-x64, linux-arm64,
     linux-riscv64, linux-ppc64/linux-ppc64le). --offline: `cargo fetch
     --locked` must have run first. RUSTFLAGS/CFLAGS/CARGO_HOME/
     CARGO_BUILD_JOBS flow in from the environment. flutter_tools passes
     CC=clang CXX=clang++ only to the cmake *configure* step; the `ninja
     install` step that runs cargo inherits the caller's environment, so
     ring's C is compiled by `cc` (gcc) unless CC is exported.
Neither mode calls rustup or dart, or touches the network. Verified for both
modes inside `unshare -rn` (no network) on ppc64le; mode 2's library came out
bit-identical (same GNU build-id) to a standalone `cargo build` with the same
flags. See REPORT.md.

The cargokit/ directory is left in place, unused on Linux.
---
diff --git a/packages/localsend_isolates/rust_builder/linux/CMakeLists.txt b/packages/localsend_isolates/rust_builder/linux/CMakeLists.txt
index 83ae241..75cf916 100644
--- a/packages/localsend_isolates/rust_builder/linux/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/packages/localsend_isolates/rust_builder/linux/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -7,13 +7,77 @@ cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.10)
 set(PROJECT_NAME "rust_lib_localsend_app")
 project(${PROJECT_NAME} LANGUAGES CXX)
 
-include("../cargokit/cmake/cargokit.cmake")
-apply_cargokit(${PROJECT_NAME} ../../rust rust_lib_localsend_app "")
+# Cargokit is bypassed here: it drives `rustup run <channel> cargo`, installs
+# toolchains/targets, `dart pub get`s its own build tool and knows no ppc64le
+# triple. Instead, either
+#   1. LOCALSEND_RUST_LIB (environment or -D) names a librust_lib_localsend_app.so
+#      that was already built with plain `cargo build` (what the PKGBUILD does),
+#      and it is bundled as is; or
+#   2. plain `cargo` from PATH (the system toolchain) is run here, offline and
+#      --locked, for the triple matching FLUTTER_TARGET_PLATFORM. RUSTFLAGS,
+#      CFLAGS, CARGO_HOME and CARGO_BUILD_JOBS come from the environment.
+if(NOT DEFINED LOCALSEND_RUST_LIB AND DEFINED ENV{LOCALSEND_RUST_LIB})
+  set(LOCALSEND_RUST_LIB "$ENV{LOCALSEND_RUST_LIB}")
+endif()
+
+if(LOCALSEND_RUST_LIB)
+  if(NOT EXISTS "${LOCALSEND_RUST_LIB}")
+    message(FATAL_ERROR "LOCALSEND_RUST_LIB=${LOCALSEND_RUST_LIB} does not exist")
+  endif()
+  set(LOCALSEND_RUST_LIB_PATH "${LOCALSEND_RUST_LIB}")
+else()
+  if(NOT FLUTTER_TARGET_PLATFORM)
+    message(FATAL_ERROR "FLUTTER_TARGET_PLATFORM is not set and LOCALSEND_RUST_LIB is not given")
+  elseif(FLUTTER_TARGET_PLATFORM STREQUAL "linux-x64")
+    set(LOCALSEND_RUST_TRIPLE "x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu")
+  elseif(FLUTTER_TARGET_PLATFORM STREQUAL "linux-arm64")
+    set(LOCALSEND_RUST_TRIPLE "aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu")
+  elseif(FLUTTER_TARGET_PLATFORM STREQUAL "linux-riscv64")
+    set(LOCALSEND_RUST_TRIPLE "riscv64gc-unknown-linux-gnu")
+  elseif(FLUTTER_TARGET_PLATFORM STREQUAL "linux-ppc64" OR FLUTTER_TARGET_PLATFORM STREQUAL "linux-ppc64le")
+    set(LOCALSEND_RUST_TRIPLE "powerpc64le-unknown-linux-gnu")
+  else()
+    message(FATAL_ERROR "No Rust triple known for FLUTTER_TARGET_PLATFORM=${FLUTTER_TARGET_PLATFORM}")
+  endif()
+
+  find_program(LOCALSEND_CARGO cargo)
+  if(NOT LOCALSEND_CARGO)
+    message(FATAL_ERROR "cargo not found in PATH")
+  endif()
+
+  # Flutter's Debug maps to cargo's dev profile; Profile and Release to release
+  # (the same mapping cargokit uses).
+  if(CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE STREQUAL "Debug")
+    set(LOCALSEND_CARGO_PROFILE_FLAG "")
+    set(LOCALSEND_CARGO_PROFILE_DIR "debug")
+  else()
+    set(LOCALSEND_CARGO_PROFILE_FLAG "--release")
+    set(LOCALSEND_CARGO_PROFILE_DIR "release")
+  endif()
+
+  set(LOCALSEND_CARGO_TARGET_DIR "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/cargo")
+  set(LOCALSEND_RUST_LIB_PATH
+    "${LOCALSEND_CARGO_TARGET_DIR}/${LOCALSEND_RUST_TRIPLE}/${LOCALSEND_CARGO_PROFILE_DIR}/librust_lib_localsend_app.so")
+
+  # The symbolic _phony_ output makes the command run on every build, as with
+  # cargokit; cargo itself decides whether anything is stale.
+  add_custom_command(
+    OUTPUT "${LOCALSEND_RUST_LIB_PATH}" "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/_phony_"
+    COMMAND "${LOCALSEND_CARGO}" build --locked --offline ${LOCALSEND_CARGO_PROFILE_FLAG}
+      --manifest-path "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/../../rust/Cargo.toml"
+      -p rust_lib_localsend_app
+      --target "${LOCALSEND_RUST_TRIPLE}"
+      --target-dir "${LOCALSEND_CARGO_TARGET_DIR}"
+    VERBATIM
+  )
+  set_source_files_properties("${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/_phony_" PROPERTIES SYMBOLIC TRUE)
+  add_custom_target("${PROJECT_NAME}_cargo" ALL DEPENDS "${LOCALSEND_RUST_LIB_PATH}")
+endif()
 
 # List of absolute paths to libraries that should be bundled with the plugin.
 # This list could contain prebuilt libraries, or libraries created by an
 # external build triggered from this build file.
 set(rust_lib_localsend_app_bundled_libraries
-  "${${PROJECT_NAME}_cargokit_lib}"
+  "${LOCALSEND_RUST_LIB_PATH}"
   PARENT_SCOPE
 )
